## dyno-diy

dyno-diy-ask = What will a dynamometer show with a small apple on it?
dyno-diy-title = A dynamometer of our own
dyno-diy-question = We make a dynamometer: a board, a strip of paper, a spring, a wire pointer and a paper-clip hook. We draw the scale ourselves — by 100 g weights. Then we hang a small apple, about a hundred grams, on it. What will the dynamometer show?
dyno-diy-choices = About 1 N
dyno-diy-choices-2 = About 100 N — the apple is 100 g, after all
dyno-diy-choices-3 = About 0.1 N
dyno-diy-setup = A board with a strip of paper, a nail, a spring of the set (25 N/m), a wire pointer, a paper-clip hook, three 100 g weights, a ruler and a pencil; a small apple, an egg in a little bag
